#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064012 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" :question/math-academy-id "e-491" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064013 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" :question/math-academy-id "e-492" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064030 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6209" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5238f9f5-c379-5b42-9354-b22ead4bcdb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296529} {:answer/id #uuid "f09d9a66-4aa4-59fd-b9a1-c5a841d35252" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{8}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296530} {:answer/id #uuid "11db2bd2-372a-5377-bfe9-944fcab80c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296531} {:answer/id #uuid "396ff835-7b38-57bb-a2fd-11644f91946f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296532} {:answer/id #uuid "998bb2a3-092d-5c86-a034-c73088604bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11db2bd2-372a-5377-bfe9-944fcab80c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296531} :answer-field/id #uuid "1604448e-2914-5acb-82b1-40e3705e0735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a7ab00b-4ffd-5138-9522-884b73ab3aa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114299" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\int \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82009b7c-4c52-5c4e-927e-787bbad8b78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\cos x - \\cos 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061229} {:answer/id #uuid "8af5d017-22b5-59a9-adb2-0221b165383e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos x - x\\sin x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061230} {:answer/id #uuid "1b0cb35d-c20a-5297-9e40-35d072a945d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\cos x + 2\\sin x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061231} {:answer/id #uuid "21e65dfd-5fec-5122-9911-d1a57b04d94b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\sin x + \\cos x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061232} {:answer/id #uuid "63d7f576-b1c6-5404-8128-d55f070b014a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 2x + x\\sin 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b0cb35d-c20a-5297-9e40-35d072a945d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\cos x + 2\\sin x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061231} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba5a6a7-4022-5f5f-ae97-c1430dbd9a5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36f423a0-7a02-5e68-b537-f427610136e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-14437" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8fd29e6-6bd9-58bc-bce7-5e3db015ceeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296557} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb13fe6-6a5c-55ce-be04-165bd5a31202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296558} {:answer/id #uuid "1d4579da-d079-5c42-a628-ce9131d8acdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296559} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d456e5-7b4a-5aa5-8c2b-81d7b4d03657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296560} {:answer/id #uuid "158c04e6-5fa0-5afc-9c15-f4849abab66b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfb13fe6-6a5c-55ce-be04-165bd5a31202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296558} :answer-field/id #uuid "614bdd30-4e23-526c-a542-60da230ead6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b21a5562-9316-51d2-a8a5-08c055537576" :question/math-academy-id "q-14449" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "132a55bc-9bd1-5b34-a7a8-796de7c9e66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "132a55bc-9bd1-5b34-a7a8-796de7c9e66f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296564} :answer-field/id #uuid "403f1cfd-ea2b-541a-8fd0-d055bf3decd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c08b1ed2-f042-58a5-a4ad-528286adb5fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-346870" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{x} & ⇒ & v={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot {e}^{x}-\\int {e}^{x}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x{e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-2{e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot {e}^{1}-0\\cdot {e}^{0})-2({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2e-2(e-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
